{
  "company": "CRONUS International Ltd.",
  "messageType": "Help.Implementation.Get",
  "status": "Success",
  "result": [
    {
      "status": "Success",
      "name": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Verify",
      "isEnabled": true,
      "filterTableNo": 0,
      "description": "Check a Bifrost Playbook without running it; findings on disabled steps are informational.",
      "selectionDescription": "Verify a Bifrost Playbook and return its findings (errors and warnings), for example an unknown message type, a missing language model role or a per-item write that no Skip If Step Failed gates. Read-only for playbook data; a language model role check leaves a Foundation message log row. Run it before Orchestrator.Playbook.Run: Read blockingErrorCount and blockingWarningCount for Run and Schedule readiness; findings on disabled steps are informational.",
      "messageDirection": "Outbound",
      "keywords": [
        "verify playbook",
        "validate playbook",
        "check playbook",
        "playbook errors",
        "playbook warnings",
        "lint playbook"
      ],
      "chargeable": true,
      "envelope": {
        "strict": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "required": false,
          "default": false,
          "description": "Optional root Boolean, default false. When true, unknown data keys are refused before execution with UnknownParameter. Do not place this option inside data."
        },
        "subject": {
          "use": "optional",
          "forms": [
            "playbook code"
          ],
          "description": "The playbook code in data.playbookCode or as subject."
        },
        "dataRequired": true,
        "version": "1.0",
        "contentType": "text/json"
      },
      "target": [
        {
          "source": "data.playbookCode",
          "form": "code",
          "description": "Read first: the Code of the playbook. Cut to 20 characters."
        },
        {
          "source": "subject",
          "form": "code",
          "description": "Used only when data.playbookCode is not sent. Cut to 20 characters."
        }
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "playbookCode",
          "type": "string",
          "required": false,
          "description": "Code of the playbook to verify (Code[20]). Required unless subject carries the code."
        }
      ],
      "response": {
        "contentType": "text/json",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "status",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Success, also when findings were returned."
          },
          {
            "name": "playbookCode",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The verified playbook code."
          },
          {
            "name": "valid",
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "True when there is no finding with severity error, including disabled steps. For Run and Schedule readiness, read blockingErrorCount and blockingWarningCount instead."
          },
          {
            "name": "errorCount",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Number of findings with severity error, including informational findings on disabled steps."
          },
          {
            "name": "warningCount",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Number of findings with severity warning, including informational findings on disabled steps."
          },
          {
            "name": "blockingErrorCount",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Number of errors excluding informational findings on disabled steps. Run and Schedule require zero, even with ignoreWarnings."
          },
          {
            "name": "blockingWarningCount",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Number of warnings excluding informational findings on disabled steps. Run and Schedule require zero unless ignoreWarnings is true."
          },
          {
            "name": "findings",
            "type": "array",
            "description": "One entry per finding, in step order; empty when the playbook is clean.",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "severity",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "error or warning. On enabled steps, an error always stops Orchestrator.Playbook.Run and the enabling of a schedule; a warning does too unless the caller sets ignoreWarnings. Findings on disabled steps are informational."
              },
              {
                "name": "stepNo",
                "type": "integer",
                "description": "The step the finding is about; 0 for a finding about the playbook as a whole."
              },
              {
                "name": "code",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Stable code of the finding, for example UnsafeForEachWrite. The codes are listed in the notes."
              },
              {
                "name": "message",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "What is wrong, in the language of the calling session (en-US or is-IS)."
              },
              {
                "name": "nextStep",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "What to do about it, in the language of the calling session."
              },
              {
                "name": "checkStepNo",
                "type": "integer",
                "description": "Only for UnsafeForEachWrite: the forEach Check step the step should be gated on."
              },
              {
                "name": "stepDisabled",
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "Only present, and true, when the step is disabled. A finding about a disabled step never blocks a run or a schedule."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "errors": [
        {
          "code": "BusinessCentralError",
          "error": "Request must include \"playbookCode\" in the data payload or as the subject.",
          "when": "Neither data.playbookCode nor subject was sent.",
          "fix": "Send the playbook code in data.playbookCode or as subject."
        },
        {
          "code": "BusinessCentralError",
          "error": "Business Central's own error text",
          "when": "No Playbook ori exists with that code (Business Central's record-not-found text).",
          "fix": "Check the code with Data.Records.Get on table Playbook ori."
        }
      ],
      "effect": {
        "effect": "read",
        "changes": "Reads the playbook, its steps and conditions, and looks up whether a language model role and the fields of a table exist; changes no playbook data and runs no step. A language model role check reads through Data.Records.Get and leaves a Foundation message log row, and is skipped inside a transaction that has already written.",
        "idempotent": true,
        "preconditions": []
      },
      "metering": {
        "chargeable": true,
        "chargedAs": "message"
      },
      "related": [
        {
          "name": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Run",
          "useInsteadWhen": "Use this to execute the playbook once blockingErrorCount and blockingWarningCount are zero (or warnings are explicitly accepted). Run verifies again and refuses a playbook that does not verify."
        },
        {
          "name": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Schedule",
          "useInsteadWhen": "Use this to put the playbook on a schedule once blockingErrorCount and blockingWarningCount are zero (or warnings are explicitly accepted). It verifies again and refuses a playbook that does not verify."
        },
        {
          "name": "Orchestrator.Workspace.Preview",
          "useInsteadWhen": "Use this to see the workspace paths a step template can reference."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "messageType": "Orchestrator.Workspace.Preview",
            "purpose": "Optional: see the @_sys and @_who paths the request templates can use."
          },
          {
            "messageType": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Verify",
            "purpose": "Read the findings of the playbook; read blockingErrorCount and blockingWarningCount, fix blocking errors, and fix blocking warnings or accept them with ignoreWarnings. Findings on disabled steps are informational."
          },
          {
            "messageType": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Run",
            "purpose": "Run it once it verifies, or use Orchestrator.Playbook.Schedule to put it on a schedule."
          }
        ]
      },
      "examples": [
        {
          "title": "Verify a playbook with an ungated write",
          "request": {
            "type": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Verify",
            "data": {
              "playbookCode": "CUST-CREDIT-CTRL"
            }
          },
          "response": {
            "status": "Success",
            "playbookCode": "CUST-CREDIT-CTRL",
            "valid": true,
            "errorCount": 0,
            "warningCount": 1,
            "blockingErrorCount": 0,
            "blockingWarningCount": 1,
            "findings": [
              {
                "severity": "warning",
                "stepNo": 40,
                "code": "UnsafeForEachWrite",
                "message": "Step 40 (Data.Records.Set) writes for every item ...",
                "nextStep": "Set Skip If Step Failed to 30 on step 40.",
                "checkStepNo": 30
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Verify a playbook with errors",
          "request": {
            "type": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Verify",
            "subject": "CUST-CREDIT-CTRL"
          },
          "response": {
            "status": "Success",
            "playbookCode": "CUST-CREDIT-CTRL",
            "valid": false,
            "errorCount": 2,
            "warningCount": 0,
            "blockingErrorCount": 2,
            "blockingWarningCount": 0,
            "findings": [
              {
                "severity": "error",
                "stepNo": 30,
                "code": "LanguageModelRoleNotFound",
                "message": "Step 30 calls LLM.Prompt.Complete with roleCode HAIKU, but this company has no language model with that code. ...",
                "nextStep": "List the codes with Data.Records.Get on table ..."
              },
              {
                "severity": "error",
                "stepNo": 50,
                "code": "StepReferenceNotFound",
                "message": "Step 50 refers to step 45 (@45...), which does not exist in this playbook. ...",
                "nextStep": "Correct the step number in the reference, or add the missing step."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "An informational error on a disabled step",
          "request": {
            "type": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Verify",
            "data": {
              "playbookCode": "DRAFT"
            }
          },
          "response": {
            "status": "Success",
            "playbookCode": "DRAFT",
            "valid": false,
            "errorCount": 1,
            "warningCount": 0,
            "blockingErrorCount": 0,
            "blockingWarningCount": 0,
            "findings": [
              {
                "severity": "error",
                "stepNo": 20,
                "code": "CheckWithoutSuccessCondition",
                "message": "Check step 20 has no Success condition, so it answers yes every time and decides nothing.",
                "nextStep": "Add a Success condition to step 20.",
                "stepDisabled": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "A clean playbook",
          "request": {
            "type": "Orchestrator.Playbook.Verify",
            "data": {
              "playbookCode": "OVERDUE-REPORT"
            }
          },
          "response": {
            "status": "Success",
            "playbookCode": "OVERDUE-REPORT",
            "valid": true,
            "errorCount": 0,
            "warningCount": 0,
            "blockingErrorCount": 0,
            "blockingWarningCount": 0,
            "findings": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "overview": "Reads a Bifröst Playbook and returns errors and warnings for configurations the engine accepts silently, without running a step. Use it before Orchestrator.Playbook.Run, Orchestrator.Playbook.Schedule or Orchestrator.Playbook.Enqueue: every finding names the step, a stable code and what to do about it. Findings on disabled steps are informational; read blockingErrorCount and blockingWarningCount for Run and Schedule readiness.",
      "notes": "Every finding has severity, stepNo, code, message and nextStep; the text is in the language of the calling session (en-US and is-IS). valid is true when no finding has severity error; errorCount and warningCount include all findings for compatibility. For Run and Schedule readiness, read blockingErrorCount and blockingWarningCount: both exclude findings on disabled steps, but include findings about the playbook as a whole. Errors always block; warnings block unless ignoreWarnings is true. Findings on disabled steps are informational. A playbook with no findings answers valid true and an empty findings array. Every step is checked, enabled or not, so a playbook built with all steps disabled can be verified before anything is switched on. A finding about a disabled step carries stepDisabled true and never blocks a run or a schedule. UnsafeForEachWrite is judged on enabled steps only. Errors: UnknownFieldReference for @N.field and @N.@_iter.field (step N does not store the field in its Result Log Paths; stored names retain their original casing and matching is case-insensitive), MessageTypeUnavailable (the step calls a message type that does not exist in this deployment or is not enabled for this user in this company; a type that exists but is not enabled is not reported on a step that has a Start condition, because the author has decided when it runs, as the reporting tail does with _who.telegramChatId Exists), TemplateNotJson (the request template is not a JSON object; the engine would send an empty request), CheckWithoutSuccessCondition (a Check step with no Success condition answers yes every time), NextStepNotFound (a Next Step edge points to a step that does not exist), IterateSourceInvalid (the forEach source step is missing or does not come first), InvalidSkipGate (Skip If Step Failed names a step that is missing, does not come first or does not iterate, so every item would be skipped), StepReferenceNotFound and StepReferenceNotEarlier (an @stepNo reference to a step that is missing or does not run before), LanguageModelRoleNotFound (the roleCode of a LLM.* step is not a language model of this company), ScheduledWithErrors (the playbook is scheduled and has errors on enabled steps). Warnings: AskForEachUnbounded (an LLM.Prompt.Ask forEach consumes a record reader without take; paging does not bound model cost), AskDataConditionWithoutSchema (an Ask Success or Error condition reads data without responseSchema), AskTraceDiscarded (includeTrace is true, but Orchestrator discards the trace before storing or using the response), AskWithoutToolsAllow (an LLM.Prompt.Ask step has no non-empty tools.allow), EmailContentNotSanitized (an Email.Draft.Set or Orchestrator.Email.Send attachment contentText, or a body with a step reference, is not the answer of an earlier Content.Html.Sanitize step), EmailLiteralRecipient (a literal address in to, cc or bcc), UnsafeForEachWrite (an enabled forEach step with a write-type message type iterates the same array as an earlier enabled forEach Check step and has Skip If Step Failed = 0; Next Step No. edges apply once per forEach step, never per item, so only Skip If Step Failed = <check step> gates the write per item), ActionWithoutSuccessCondition (an Action with no Success condition counts as successful whenever the type does not raise, also when it answers status Error), ForEachSourceUnguarded (a record reader that feeds a forEach has no Success condition on noOfRecords, so an empty answer still succeeds and the forEach does nothing), UnknownFieldReference (@_current.fields.X names a field the source table does not have or returns under primaryKey; these @_current findings remain warnings). A write-type message type is one whose last name segment is Set, Post, Delete, Create, Update, Insert, Modify, Cancel, Correct, Send, MakeOrder, Release, Reopen, Approve, Reject, Register, Schedule or Enqueue. A record reader is a Data.* type ending in Get, Find, Search or List. The roleCode of a LLM.* step is looked up with Data.Records.Get on the Bifrost Language Model table, because the language models belong to Bifrost Bragi, which Bifrost Orchestrator does not depend on. When the table cannot be read (Bragi is not installed, or the caller may not read it) the check says nothing. Fields are looked up in the table metadata; a table that cannot be resolved is not judged. An operator that is not an AL name cannot be stored (Operator is an enum), so it is not a finding. Orchestrator.Playbook.Run and Orchestrator.Playbook.Schedule (and the Schedule action of the playbook card) verify first. They refuse with PreconditionFailed, naming the findings in the answer, when an enabled step has an error, or a warning unless the request sets ignoreWarnings to true; ignoreWarnings never waives an error, including an unknown stored-field reference that previously only warned. A run started by the Job Queue is not verified again."
    }
  ],
  "conventions": {
    "errorsAndWarnings": "## Errors and warnings\r\nAn error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.\r\nWhen a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.\r\nRequest values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.\r\nRequest values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `\"1234.56\"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.\r\nAnswers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.\r\nBoth success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.\r\n`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {\"type\":\"Memory.User.Set\",\"strict\":true,\"data\":{\"memory\":\"test\",\"memry\":\"typo\"}} is refused.\r\n`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.\r\nFeature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.\r\nA message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.\r\n`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is \"no concurrent lock on the same records\"; `nextStep` is \"Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed.\" Bifrost does not retry automatically. Uncaught recognized lock errors are also `Retryable` for `write` types. Uncaught `read` and `irreversible` errors remain `BusinessCentralError`, because an irreversible operation may already have committed.\r\n`ConfirmationRequired` is the preview refusal for an irreversible type called without `expectedCount`. Nothing was changed; inspect `expected` and the description before sending the same request with that count. `ConfirmationMismatch` means the count has changed or the sent count was wrong; nothing was changed. Inspect the new preview before confirming again. Feature apps may implement `Msg Confirm ori` or call public `Confirm Gate ori.Confirm` to use the same protocol.\r\nCodes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`, `ConfirmationRequired`, `ConfirmationMismatch`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.\r\n"
  }
}
